[45.781, "o", "    \"answer\": \"I'm not a doctor. For high glucose or pre-diabetes the LiveWell guides recommend steady, sustainable food habits rather than crash diets. Build meals with the Healthy Plate: half vegetables and fruit, one quarter wholegrains or staples, and one quarter protein (fish, chicken, tofu, eggs, beans). Choose wholegrains more often (brown rice, oats, wholemeal bread), keep carbohydrate portions sensible and spread them across the day, and always pair carbs with protein and vegetables. Use simple portion cues: a palm-sized protein, a fist-sized staple, and two handfuls of vegetables. Swap sugary drinks for water, kopi kosong or siew dai, and cut sauces/gravy where possible. Make small changes (one habit at a time) and see a doctor or dietitian to personalise your plan and follow up on the high result.\",\r\n"]
